    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d271">

                <pb facs="0288" n="214" xml:id="pg214"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/857</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Page</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-27T11:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 27, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 4.30 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1100. I learn that the Vatican having expressed to Central Empires’ Governments
                    surprise that recent replies omitted reference to points in Pope’s letter
                    regarding restoration of Belgium and occupied French territory received
                    yesterday evening reply saying that Germany stands on Reichstag resolutions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Nelson Page</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
